# TypeScript

- `strict` stays on. No `any`. No `as unknown as`.
- Prefer typed arrays / object pools over class-per-entity.
- Gameplay constants that designers will tune belong in `web/src/data/` or `web/src/config.ts`, not magic numbers in `update()`.
- Keep functions small. One file = one job (`director.ts`, not `gameplay.ts`).
